==Strategy==
This stage features a relentless, yet timer-based flood of annoying ranged [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies. As such, it is recommended to utilize strong [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] to destroy the base as quickly as possible. In particular, close-ranged rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]], as well as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] are all good options for this stage. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is an accessible, spammable rusher with [[Area Attack|Area Attacks]] that can help break through the Dolphinas, though he struggles somewhat against the Mr. Moles.

In {{4c}}, since Manic Lion Cat is no longer usable, using [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] with Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]] works, so long as some support with Courier Cat or other fast attackers is provided.

